          "path": "tests/providers/test_anthropic_closed_world_http.py",
          "line": 230,
          "end_line": 230
        }
      ],
      "mechanism": "_consume_protocol_stream retains the actual iterator timeout/cancellation, but evaluate_bytes first calls decode_sse without transport-termination context. decode_sse finalizes pending data as InvalidFrame(EVENT_DELIMITER_MISSING). The absorbing PROTOCOL_INVALID state is installed before the stored TIMEOUT/CANCELLATION event is stepped.",
      "reproduction": "Run .venv/Scripts/python.exe -B C:\\小说\\shared-anthropic-closed-world-offline-20260905-v1\\reviews\\reviewer-1-synthetic-repro.py from the repository root. It uses the production AnthropicAdapter.complete and httpx.MockTransport with only synthetic protocol bytes and a metadata-only capture observer.",
      "observed_preterminal": "message_start + content_block_start + a content_block_delta truncated inside its text string, then ReadTimeout or CancelledError: public failure is ProviderResponseCaptureError(EVENT_DELIMITER_MISSING); owner.primary_cause is PROTOCOL_INVALID; original transport exception identity is lost.",
      "observed_postterminal": "A fully closed valid message_stop followed by event: ping/data: {type:ping} lacking only the final delimiter, then ReadTimeout or CancelledError: trace first reaches SEMANTIC_SUCCESS_TERMINAL, then becomes PROTOCOL_INVALID_TERMINAL; no ModelResponse is returned; capture transport_complete is false.",
      "expected": "An unfinished frame due to the known interrupted read needs an explicit source-grounded boundary decision. Before semantic terminal, timeout/cancellation remains the primary transport cause. An interrupted nonsemantic ping tail must not revoke the complete semantic result. A completed invalid semantic frame remains a separate fail-closed case.",
      "master_requirements_violated": [
        "0 precise failure-cause preservation",
        "4 actual production protocol domain",
        "7 post-terminal timeout/cancel invariants",
        "8 D/E timeout/cancellation before terminal",
        "11/14 generated state/fault proof completeness"
      ],
      "evidence_contract_contradiction": "domain-final/shared-stream-causal-precedence-contract-v1.json claims preterminal transport interruption preserves the original exception instance. Both preterminal reproductions contradict that claim.",
      "coverage_gap": "The 176-cell matrix begins after framing. FaultWire divides bytes into 11-byte chunks but raises only after delivering the entire supplied raw buffer; the success fault cases supply delimiter-complete wire(COMPLETE + PING*n). Chunking alone does not test transport termination inside a frame. A 100_PERCENT state-machine fault claim cannot establish the shared framing/lifecycle boundary for these reachable inputs.",
      "risk": "Ordinary timeout/cancellation can be misreported as a protocol defect; a fully available successful response can be discarded when only its ping tail is interrupted. This recreates the shared terminal-tail incident family despite green event-boundary tests.",
      "disposition": "STOP. Shared boundary architecture proof is rejected. This review does not authorize a narrow patch or another patch-and-retry campaign."
    }
  ],
